  "grade": "9-10",
  "learningGoal": "Find the distance between two points using d = √((x₂-x₁)² + (y₂-y₁)²).",
  "spokenLines": [
    "Distance between two points.",
    "The formula is d equals the square root of x two minus x one, squared, plus y two minus y one, squared.",
    "Let's find the distance from one comma two to four comma six.",
    "Plot both points.",
    "x two minus x one is three. Y two minus y one is four.",
    "So d equals root of three squared plus four squared.",
    "Nine plus sixteen is twenty five.",
    "Root twenty five is five. Distance is five."
  ],
